<title>GERMANY: AMV says 1996 premium income up 1.6 pct.</title>
<headline>AMV says 1996 premium income up 1.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>AACHEN, Germany 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>German insurer Aachener und Muenchener Versichering AG (AMV) said on Wednesday that its 1996 gross premium income rose by 1.6 percent to around 2.0 billion marks ($1.2 billion).</p>
<p>The firm also said it expected its 1997 profits to be sufficient to allow an unchanged dividend payout this year, and said its first quarter 1997 premium income was at the same level as a year earlier.</p>
<p>($ = 1.712 German Marks)</p>
